    2. Place the template on the 22x22 grid at a random position
    3. Place 1-2 partial copies (support cells identical, yellow positions filled with yellow) at non-overlapping positions -- these form the output state
    4. Scatter 47-85 distractor pixels (blue and azure) randomly on empty cells; after placement, verify no accidental 3x3 support-pattern matches exist (reject or remove offending pixels)
    5. Derive input by replacing yellow fill-mask cells in each partial copy with black (template itself keeps its yellow)
